depgraph: slot-operator probes pass over lower versions before creating packages

Sub-series: A (probe, match and config memos) - patch 7 of 10; applies to 3.0.83 with only the earlier patches of this sub-series.
Ported to upstream 73646c35d: adapted: not_older_than is added after upstream's new selectable_built parameter of _iter_similar_available(); _iter_similar_available_imp() takes selectable_built (default False) before newer_than/or_equal; the bounded scans always run with selectable_built False, as their callers did. The loops of _slot_operator_update_probe and _downgrade_probe, on which the bound argument rests, are unchanged upstream

_upgrade_available(pkg) is true only if some candidate compares greater
than pkg, and the loops of _slot_operator_update_probe skip every candidate
that is less than the package they replace unless _downgrade_probe() is
true. Yet each scan created a Package (metadata, masks, USE) for every
version of the cp. The scans now pass over a candidate cpv with a lower
version before a Package is made for it (newer_than / not_older_than in
_iter_match_pkgs_atom_imp). _iter_replacement_parents and
_iter_replacement_children yield the bounded sequence first and fall back
to the complete one when the bounded one cannot settle the question (it
yielded nothing, or nothing from the child's slot). Creating a Package has
one visible effect, a repeated config warning for "+flag" values, so the
bound is switched off once such a warning has been printed
(_probe_bounds_allowed reads config._regenerate_warned).

On top of patches 0001-0013, resolve seconds before -> after
(median of the runs, at least 2 per figure):
  start 41.2 -> 37.6, holds 23.5 -> 19.7, masks 44.5 -> 42.0,
  py313 27.0 -> 23.1, bdeps 31.9 -> 28.3, policykit 24.0 -> 20.1
  sum of six 192.2 -> 170.8 (-21.4 s, -4.8 % of the stock sum 447.5)
Patches 0001-0014 together: 447.5 -> 170.8 s (-62 %); 447.5 is the
stock sum of the ladder run of 2026-11-20, stock was not run again here.

Weak spots and what was not checked:
* The argument for skipping lower versions is in the two docstrings and
  depends on how _downgrade_probe is defined; a change there must revisit
  it. Configurations that print config warnings never take the bounded path,
  so they were not exercised by the six states.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20..21. Not a human-written
change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of
one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the same merge list
in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts and the same
package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
